    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Barry Auctioneers & Valuers are delighted to present to the market this charming three-bedroom mid-terrace property, dating from circa 1900. Full of character and period charm, the home retains many of its original features, including impressive high ceilings and a traditional laneway entrance.\r\n\r\nIdeally located in the heart of Cork City, the property is tucked away in a quiet cul-de-sac while remaining within easy walking distance of the city centre and a wide range of local amenities, including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and public transport links.\r\n\r\nWhile the property would benefit from modernisation and refurbishment, it offers an exciting opportunity for a purchaser to create a wonderful city-centre home while retaining the charm and character of a period property.\r\n\r\nWith its excellent location, generous potential and wealth of original features, this property would make an ideal dream home or investment opportunity.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the potential and character this property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway - 8.22m x 1.84m \r\n\r\n\r\nLiving Room - 3.96m x 3.86m \r\nOpen Fire Place\r\n\r\nKitchen - 3.66m x 3.22m \r\n\r\n\r\nDownstairs WC - 1.62m x 1.48m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 4.21m x 3.93m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.94m x 3.28m \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 3.94m x 2.83m \r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom - 3.36m x 3.22m \r\n\r\n\r\nOutside garden - \r\nLarge front garden & Enclosed rear garden\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "5 minute walk to the city\r\nClose to all local amenities \r\nOriginal high ceilings feature in the house\r\nQuiet cul -de -sac area\r\nFully enclosed rear yard\r\nSouth facing aspect"
